Source: pg-clickhouse
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Yandex MDB Team <mdb@yandex-team.ru>
Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 10),
               postgresql-server-dev-all (>= 195~),
               cmake (>= 3.12),
               libcurl4-openssl-dev,
               libssl-dev,
               g++,
               pkg-config
Standards-Version: 1.1-0
Homepage: https://github.com/ClickHouse/pg_clickhouse

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-clickhouse
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, postgresql-PGVERSION
Description: PostgreSQL Foreign Data Wrapper for ClickHouse
 pg_clickhouse is a PostgreSQL extension that implements a Foreign Data
 Wrapper (FDW) for ClickHouse. It allows querying ClickHouse tables
 directly from PostgreSQL using standard SQL.
 .
 Features include full SELECT pushdown, aggregate pushdown, INSERT support,
 and both HTTP and binary protocol drivers.
